.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-INSTALL-STATUS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-install-status
.Nd one line saying whether an install is alive, and how far it has got
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl w | -watch
.Op Fl v | -verbose
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The installer logs when a phase starts, and its longest phases \(em the
package passes, the ZFS module build \(em then work for minutes in
silence, which reads as a hang.
.Nm
answers
.Dq is it still going
in one line, from what the installer already writes: the phase, out of
six, and what it is doing; how many packages the new system has; how much
the pool holds; and how long it has been running.
A field that cannot be read is left out rather than guessed.
If the log has a
.Ql FATAL
line, that line is printed instead and the exit status is 1.
.Pp
On an installed machine it says when the machine was installed, from the
install manifest.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl w , Fl -watch
Repaint the line every five seconds until the autoinstall unit stops.
.It Fl v , Fl -verbose
Add a second line naming the phases finished.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev KLDLOAD_POOL
The pool whose size is shown; default
.Ql rpool .
.It Ev KLDLOAD_TARGET_MNT
Where the new system is mounted; default
.Pa /target .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/log/installer/autoinstall.log
The unattended installer's log, on the live system.
.It Pa /root/kldload-install-logs/
The copy left on the installed system.
.It Pa /etc/kldload/install-manifest.env
What was installed, and when.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1n -compact
.It 0
Running, finished, or installed.
.It 1
The install failed.
.It 2
A usage error.
.It 3
The install log cannot be read here; run as root.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
On a kldload desktop on 2026-09-30:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kldload-install-status
installed fedora desktop on 2026-08-30T13:48:59Z — nothing is installing now
# (exited 0)
$ kldload-install-status
no install log readable as anthony — run as root
# (exited 3)
.Ed
.Pp
During an unattended install, on the machine being installed; not run for
this page:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kldload-install-status --watch
# one line, repainted: [phase/6] what it is doing · packages · pool size · elapsed
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kldload-autoinstall 8 ,
.Xr kldload-install-target 8
.Sh HISTORY
Written after 2026-09-11, when an operator watching three healthy installs
read the silence as a hang each time, once on a machine that had already
finished and passed every smoke test.
.Pp
On 2026-09-30, writing this page: on a desktop a month after its install
it printed
.Ql [1/6] starting  ·  2323 pkgs  ·  1.61T  ·  43952m23s ,
reading an interactive install's log as if it were an unattended one in
progress; and as a user it said nothing had ever run on the machine,
because the log under
.Pa /root
could not be read.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
The phases are read from the unattended installer's console log; an
install made interactively leaves no such log, and has no live line to
show.
